# =============================================================================
# Datasets & Auto-Generated CSVs
# See docs/07_dataset.md for dataset download instructions
# =============================================================================
# The whole data tree is ignored — images, labels, annotations and all.
# Nothing under data/ is version-controlled, so keep your own backup of it:
#   data/detector/final_*_labels.csv   bounding-box annotations for 58,361 images
#   data/detector/label_map.json       class name -> integer label
#   data/yolo/data.yaml                YOLO dataset config
# These were tracked until 2026-08-04 and remain recoverable from git history:
#   git show <commit>:data/detector/final_train_labels.csv > <path>
data/

# Auto-generated config (written by train.py at startup)
data_fixed.yaml

# =============================================================================
# Model Weights & Exported Artifacts (Pretrained, Checkpoints & ExecuTorch/ONNX)
# =============================================================================
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.ptl
*.pte
*.tflite
*.engine
*.bin
*.safetensors
yolo*.pt
models/*
!models/.gitkeep
!models/README.md

# =============================================================================
# Training Outputs, Runs & Logs
# =============================================================================
outputs/*
# …except the cross-model comparison artifacts: they are paper figures and tables,
# they are small (~128 KB), and docs/ links to them — an ignored path would render
# as a broken image on GitHub. Git needs each parent un-ignored before a nested
# negation can apply, hence the stepwise rules.
!outputs/benchmarks/
outputs/benchmarks/*
!outputs/benchmarks/*.md
!outputs/benchmarks/*.json
!outputs/benchmarks/figures/
outputs/benchmarks/figures/*
!outputs/benchmarks/figures/*.png
runs/
logs/
*.log

# RT-DETR generated data yaml
data_rtdetr.yaml

# Versioned weight snapshots (scripts/archive_weights.py) — large binaries
weights/
